From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 03:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP: fix same-band MLD reauthentication state

An MLD station can start a new authentication exchange on the same band
without first tearing down its old association. Management frames then
carry the new link address while the station object is still keyed by its
MLD address.

Use the per-exchange link address for asynchronous FT and FILS replies and
as the indication that the current authentication is an MLD exchange. Clear
it when a legacy authentication starts on a station that still has an MLD
profile. Do not overwrite the profile of an authorized PMF station until it
is actually eligible to be replaced.

A previous failed authentication may also leave an independent WPA state
machine on a partner link. Free those stale state machines before installing
the new MLD profile, while preserving an authorized PMF association.

This is adapted to the upstream hostapd MLO station model and complements
the peer-link Authentication reply and TX status fixes already present in
this tree.

Based on Qualcomm's same-band MLD reconnect, MLD profile overwrite, and
failed partner authentication fixes.

Co-developed-by: Ramasamy Kaliappan <rkaliapp@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Ramasamy Kaliappan <rkaliapp@qti.qualcomm.com>
Co-developed-by: Sowmiya Sree Elavalagan <ssreeela@qti.qualcomm.com>
